WEBVTT

00:00.900 --> 00:02.600
<v You>Okay— what's everyone up to?

00:02.750 --> 00:07.460
<v Pointe>Billing's done with the retry fix. Docs is idle. Shop has a PR up.

00:07.660 --> 00:14.370
<v You>Great. Billing, add a test for the timeout. Docs, update the changelog. And api, bump the retry budget to five.

00:14.270 --> 00:17.060
<v Pointe>Sent, sent, and sent.

00:17.960 --> 00:19.170
<v You>Let's focus on billing.

00:19.220 --> 00:21.840
<v Pointe>Billing. Everything you say goes there.

00:22.140 --> 00:23.940
<v You>Hm— should the retries go through a queue?

00:24.640 --> 00:31.890
<v Pointe>Billing says a queue risks duplicate charges on failover. It suggests backoff with jitter, capped at ten seconds.

00:31.840 --> 00:33.290
<v You>Ten's too long for checkout.

00:33.790 --> 00:36.990
<v Pointe>Then a five second cap, with an idempotency key.

00:37.090 --> 00:38.350
<v You>Yeah. Do that.

00:38.350 --> 00:39.140
<v Pointe>Sent to billing.

00:40.040 --> 00:43.880
<v You>Okay, back to orchestrator mode. Walk me through the PR shop opened.

00:44.180 --> 00:56.080
<v Pointe>Orchestrator mode. Shop's PR makes the flaky checkout test wait for the mock gateway, instead of sleeping. The risk: it touches a shared fixture. Check the two tests that reuse it.

00:56.180 --> 00:57.590
<v You>Does it change any production code?

00:57.840 --> 00:59.350
<v Pointe>No. Tests only.
